    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (83.49) and **James Wood** (76.28) anchoring the lineup, both serving as our strongest plays. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime leadoff spot against Keller, where his speed profile remains our most critical asset in the quest for stolen bases; despite a slight discount for the catcher\u2019s arm, his elite raw projection carries him to the top of our board. Similarly, **James Wood** finds himself in an ideal position against Scherzer. While facing a veteran, the xERA of 5.89 is highly inviting, and **James Wood**\u2019s elite 0.420 xwOBA combined with a favorable park shift allows him to capitalize on the pitcher's slower delivery to the plate\u2014a massive green light for our SB-weighted strategy. **Jose Caballero** (76.02) rounds out our elite tier, as his high dynamic platoon edge against Schultz makes him a must-start despite batting seventh.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was balancing the upside of **Tyler Soderstrom** (55.04) against the bench depth. **Tyler Soderstrom** narrowly secured the final starting OF spot due to a +10% park factor adjustment that outweighed the cooling effect of facing Tolle. He outperformed our depth chart, including prospects like **Travis Bazzana** and **Edwin Arroyo**, who remain on the fringes as we monitor their transition to consistent playing time. We continue to manage our remaining roster assets\u2014**Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014as \"break glass in case of emergency\" options while keeping a close eye on the health of **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL. \n\nThe lineup is largely finalized, though we remain vigilant regarding weather and late lineup changes. We are exercising caution with **Austin Riley** (54.19), whose score is suppressed by a negative park factor and an elite catcher matchup; he is currently at the bottom of our start-worthy threshold. Meanwhile, **Zach McKinstry** (50.03) must navigate a tough hold-SP scenario, but his floor remains high enough to warrant a start given the specific categorical needs of our 5x5 build today. With **Mickey Moniak** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** currently sidelined by scheduling, we are fully committed to this active unit to maximize our daily efficiency score.",
